From 06f662c616f550caa83db9c0d774c24c66122ce2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mirko Brombin <9479903+mirkobrombin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 19:34:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] mm: admit cgroup domains across four reserved resources

Add an atomic cgroup-v2 admission ioctl over capacity, read bandwidth, write bandwidth, and queue slots. Apply the normative 20 percent headroom, retain non-preemptible reservations behind a domain fd, and roll the complete vector back on any failure.

Transition dependent admitted domains to AT_RISK before an FD-scoped provider drains. Publish the five frozen tracepoint schemas and emit deterministic admission and provider-loss SLO transitions.

Evidence: Linux 7.1.3 CONFIG_MTS_TIER=y make -j4 mm/mts.o mm/mts_tier.o.
Signed-off-by: Mirko Brombin <9479903+mirkobrombin@users.noreply.github.com>
---
